From 9bc76964688ebd1c7fa5862f3b9d4d270067fb3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:17:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: add SM8650 support

Eliza and SM8650 describe the USB3-DP combo PHY with the
"qcom,sm8650-qmp-usb3-dp-phy" compatible. Without a driver for it,
fixup_qcom_dwc3 strips the USB 3 PHY from the controller and forces
maximum-speed = "high-speed", so the fastboot gadget enumerates at USB
2.0 speed on the host:

  /sys/bus/usb/devices/3-10 speed=480 version= 2.00

Add the SM8650 configuration with the SM8550 USB3 init tables and the
v6 PCS register offsets, as Linux uses for this PHY.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
